Subject: [PATCH 3/6] wayland: A subsurface that follows the depth gets the limits

A window's depth states are made from its top-level surface: StereoDepthStates
watches that surface's stereoDepthFollowed() and nothing else. A declared
subsurface (the 3D area of an ordinary Wayland window) that asked for
kde_stereo_depth_v1 after its window was shown therefore got no state, and so no
depth_limits, until something else (a move, a change of the limits) made the
update run. The follow is now announced up the tree of subsurfaces to the top
level, so the update that tells the new follower comes at once.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
---
--- a/src/wayland/stereocontent_v1.cpp
+++ b/src/wayland/stereocontent_v1.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include "display.h"
 #include "effect/globals.h"
+#include "subcompositor.h"
 #include "surface.h"
 #include "surface_p.h"
 
@@ -49,7 +50,13 @@
     SurfaceInterface *surf = SurfaceInterface::get(surface);
     auto depth = new StereoDepthSurfaceV1(resource->client(), id, resource->version(), surf);
     SurfaceInterfacePrivate::get(surf)->stereoDepths.append(depth);
-    Q_EMIT surf->stereoDepthFollowed();
+    // the window's depth states are made from its top-level surface: a subsurface that starts
+    // following later is announced up to the top-level, so the update that tells it comes
+    for (SurfaceInterface *followed = surf; followed;) {
+        Q_EMIT followed->stereoDepthFollowed();
+        const SubSurfaceInterface *sub = followed->subSurface();
+        followed = sub ? sub->parentSurface() : nullptr;
+    }
     // a surface whose state is known tells a new follower at once
     if (const auto state = SurfaceInterfacePrivate::get(surf)->stereoDepthState) {
         depth->sendState(state->awake, state->outputEdges, state->sunk, state->popped);
